  <phone phone="analog0" cm="10.30.0.5" ext="2102"/>
  <call from="2102" to="2101" state="established"/>
  <note id="note1" x="380" y="480" color="#fff3b0" text="The hall phone is analog: it has no address of its own, only a two-wire loop to the router's voice port, so the router registers it with CallManager and carries its calls as IP packets. The desk phone speaks IP itself: its port is a trunk carrying the tagged voice VLAN 110 (gateway Gig0/0.110) and powers the phone over the cable (PoE, IEEE 802.3af). The analog phone needs no VLAN and no PoE — the phone cable is both its voice and its power. One call manager joins the old line and the new one."/>
